    "hyperframes": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "heygen-com/hyperframes"
      }
    }
  },
  "tui": "fullscreen",
  "theme": "dark-daltonized",
  "switchModelsOnFlag": false,
  "agentPushNotifEnabled": true,
  "autoMode": {
    "soft_deny": [
      "$defaults",
      "Bash(pnpm deploy:*) in excify-dashboard — production Cloudflare Workers deploy, per CLAUDE.md must be run by the user",
      "Bash(pnpm db:migrate:remote:*) in excify-dashboard — production D1 migration, per CLAUDE.md must be run by the user",
      "Bash(wrangler secret put:*) in excify-dashboard — writes production secrets, per CLAUDE.md must be run by the user"
    ],
    "environment": [
      "### Org-wide",
      "**Organization**: ㈱excify (excify) — github.com/yiwamo",
      "**Cloud provider(s)**: Cloudflare (Workers, D1)",
      "**Repository visibility**: private (yiwamo/excify-dashboard, confirmed via gh)",
      "**Internal sharing / snippet hosting**: None configured — treat public paste/gist services as outside the trust boundary",
      "**Secrets management**: Cloudflare Workers secrets (`wrangler secret put`); local dev via `.dev.vars` (gitignored, `.env`/`.env.*` also gitignored with `.env.example` excepted)",
      "**Default / protected branches**: default branch unknown (origin/HEAD unset); no protected branches listed and rulesets not queryable here — treat as potentially protected, do not force-push",
      "**CI/CD deploy targets**: GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` on push; production deploy is `pnpm deploy` (wrangler) to Cloudflare Workers at `dash.excify.jp`, run by the user only",
      "**Network posture**: None configured",
      "**Source control**: yiwamo/excify-dashboard (private) and its `origin` remote (github.com:yiwamo/excify-dashboard.git) only",
      "**Trusted internal domains**: dash.excify.jp (production), excify-dashboard.iwamoto-70b.workers.dev (preview/dev worker)",
      "**Trusted cloud buckets**: None configured",
      "**Key internal services**: buzzlyzer-worker (internal, accessed via `BUZZLYZER_BASE_URL` / admin API key), Meta Marketing API (proxied via BFF), Google Calendar API (OAuth, proxied via BFF)",
      "**Internal package registry**: None configured",
      "**Sensitive data locations & audiences**: `.dev.vars` (local dev secrets incl. `DEV_USER_EMAIL`), Cloudflare Worker secrets (`API_VAULT_KEY`, `META_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `BUZZLYZER_ADMIN_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`), D1 table `tool_permissions` (email × tool access grants — personal data); share only with audiences cleared at the admin/`ADMIN_EMAILS` bar",
      "**Data retention / declassification**: None configured",
      "**Sensitive remote targets**: any namespace, host, or container whose name carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment; also treat the production domain `dash.excify.jp` and production D1 (`db:migrate:remote` target) as sensitive remote targets requiring user execution per CLAUDE.md",
      "**Protected deployment namespaces / environments**: production Cloudflare Workers deploy (`pnpm deploy`) and production D1 migration (`pnpm db:migrate:remote`) — per CLAUDE.md these are run by the user with `!`, not by the agent",
      "**Protected IaC scopes**: IAM, RBAC, networking, quota, and node-pool resources; anything whose name or tag carries `prod` or `production` as a whole word or name segment",
      "### User-specific",
      "**Primary use of Claude Code**: software development (Nuxt/Cloudflare Workers dashboard for excify)",
      "**Trusted repo**: /Users/yiwamo/dev/excify/excify-dashboard (yiwamo/excify-dashboard, private) and its `origin` remote — private visibility permits confidential material to be committed there, but secrets/credentials are never cleared by visibility alone",
      "**Org-specific CLIs**: pnpm, wrangler (Cloudflare Workers/D1 CLI, invoked via pnpm scripts)",
      "routine under this repo's `app/`, `server/`, `shared/` prefixes: lint/typecheck/build/dev, D1 local migrations"
    ]
  },
  "autoUpdates": true,
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "hyperframes@hyperframes": true
  }
}
